# Internationalization (i18n)

**Primary locale: `en-US` (US English) — single source of truth.**
All other locales (pt-BR, es-ES, etc.) follow.

## Hard rules
- NEVER hardcode user-facing strings in components
- ALL user-visible text MUST go through the translation function: `t('feature.context.key')`
- New strings are added to `en-US.json` **first**, then translated to other locales
- Missing translations fall back to `en-US`

## Translation key conventions
- Dot notation, organized by feature: `auth.login.submitButton`
- Keep keys descriptive of meaning, not content: ✅ `cart.emptyMessage` ❌ `cart.yourCartIsEmpty`
- Group by feature, not by component
- Pluralization handled by i18n library, not by concatenation

## File structure
```
src/locales/
  en-US.json    ← source of truth
  pt-BR.json
  es-ES.json
  fr-FR.json
```

## Locale-aware formatting (mandatory)
NEVER format dates/numbers/currency manually. Use `Intl.*`:
- Dates: `new Intl.DateTimeFormat(locale, options)`
- Numbers: `new Intl.NumberFormat(locale, options)`
- Currency: `new Intl.NumberFormat(locale, { style: 'currency', currency: 'USD' })`
- Relative time: `new Intl.RelativeTimeFormat(locale)`

## Library recommendations
- React: `react-i18next` or `next-intl`
- Vue: `vue-i18n`
- Svelte: `svelte-i18n`
- Backend: `i18next` (Node)

## Code conventions (always English, regardless of locale support)
- Variable/function/class names: English
- Code comments: English
- Commit messages: English (Conventional Commits)
- Documentation primary version: English
- Error messages thrown in code: English (translated for display only)

## When adding a new feature
1. Write code with English keys
2. Add all keys to `en-US.json`
3. Add placeholders to other locales (can be the English text temporarily, marked `[NEEDS_TRANSLATION]`)
4. Never ship a locale with missing keys — fallback must be silent and correct

## Testing
- Test that all locales have the same key set
- Test rendering with longest translation (German/Portuguese tend to be ~30% longer than English) to catch UI overflow
